wn, with nobody at the door confirming it arrived."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A status page shows a memory write as applied because the sending step ran, although nothing observed the write arriving.","does_not_prove":"Confirming arrival at the named receivers leaves every other declared effect unconfirmed and still marked as such.","enforced_in_component_ids":["durable_agent_work_landing_replay","agent_route_observability_runtime"],"example":{"component_ids":["durable_agent_work_landing_replay"],"text":"The work-landing replay confirms that an agent's change was actually saved at its destination before showing it as landed."},"governs":"Displays of what an action reached.","plain":"The mistake of showing where an action was meant to go as if it had already arrived there, when nothing checked that it reached the receiving end.","potential_misread":"That knowing where something is going is as good as seeing it arrive.","refuses":"Showing a declared, inferred or generated destination as an observed effect with no evidence that the effect happened.","requires":"An observation of the effect at the receiving end, or else the destination shown as declared and unobserved.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"Readers can tell 'sent towards a known destination' apart from 'confirmed as arrived'."},"rests_on":[],"source_ref":"ANTI_PRINCIPLES.md::AP-16","statement":"| ID | Violated axioms | Rejected failure shape |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| AP-16 Receiver inflation | AX-8, AX-12 | Displaying a declared, inferred or generated downstream target as an effect observed at runtime, with no evidence that the effect happened. |","statement_sha256":"c1ceca914b11ce24f0e90e1211b3830be55c825a5919d94799e6f47c1f122a98","title":"Receiver inflation","violates":["AX-8","AX-12"]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}